5. E5 OWNERSHIP AND ZERO-OPERATION LAW

The accepted canonical E6 reports bind one fresh public E5 collection to each
independent top-level Living or Conformance report. Living passes the same
publicly validated canonical E5 report to the shared Conformance builder. The
shared builder validates and renders that received report but collects E5 zero
times. Canonical SHA-256 and byte counts agree across the top-level and shared
receipts.

  DIRECT_CONFORMANCE_E5_COLLECTOR_CALLS=1
  LIVING_E5_COLLECTOR_CALLS=1
  LIVING_SHARED_CONFORMANCE_BUILDER_E5_COLLECTOR_CALLS=0
  SECOND_DELTA_RUNTIME_CALLS=0
  GLOBAL_OR_PROCESS_CACHE_REUSE=0
  TEST_FIXTURE_SUBSTITUTION=0
  PRIVATE_G2D_CALLS=0
  RECONSTRUCTED_E5_CASES=0

The current report fields and validators require zero provider, model,
network, connector, external-DRS, ActionCommitPacket, permission, receipt,
FinalOutput, DRS-write, authority, and real-world-effect counts. G2-E selects
bounded recomputation and evidence; it creates no Root authority.

